  "note": "Defence on a canal (IC s85 pp 449-458; IBB S60-62 pp 328-339, Annex V p 483 / App 8 p 484; the C Pen posns after IBB S57 Fig 34 p 317). Plan metres from the Bn centre, y toward the enemy; the click (the pivot) is on the canal in front of the centre. A and B Coys on the home bank (defences on the obstacle itself near the border: IC s85 para 10 b), their front edge 70 m from the water's centre (E); C and D Coys in depth about 3000 m back from the obstacle (greater depth than normal, IBB S61 para 7 p 333; Annex V draws 1830-2750 m); counter penetration posns AA, BB, CC covering the gap between the forward Coys and the flanks, occupied when ordered (Fig 34, para 25: dashed), and the prepared alternative positions in depth (IC s85 para 12 a); mask posns for some major weapons ahead of the obstacle (IC s85 para 7 p 454), by day 300-500 m ahead of the main posn (IC s85 para 28 b p 462; AMP p 88; canal.maskAheadM): laid 400 m beyond it; minefields on the far side and in the gap on the home side (para 17 a), double concertina on both banks (para 17 b). With the terrain the plan is laid along the canal the click is on (MovementGuideWater.readWater), and the defence is checked as any other: the En approaches cross the canal only at its bridges and fords. Bn HQ (IBB S3 pp 22-24; p 23: placed centrally within the Bn locality, preferably behind the depth localities; a defended locality of 55 all ranks, concealed from the air, dug in, near the Bde axis with an alternative posn; laid about 500 m behind the rearmost depth / reserve Coy (the distance a decision, E). The RRs, a section of two in each rifle Coy, sited first in the forward localities with an alternative each 200-300 m back (IBB S8 pp 38-42; IC p 367).",
